# Wire shape

The shape of a JSON document, checked once and whole before anything is read
from it, so a document is never half-read. A specification lists `name:kind`
fields; the kinds are `text`, `int`, `bool`, `texts` (strings), `object`, `array`,
`opttext` and `optint` (the value or `null`), and `any`.

## Note
The kind of a `name:kind` specification (`any` when it names none).

## To fieldKind (spec: Text) -> Text:
    Let parts be split(spec, ":").
    If length of parts is at least 2:
        Return item 2 of parts.
    Return "any".

## Note
The name of a specification.

## To fieldName (spec: Text) -> Text:
    Return item 1 of split(spec, ":").

## Note
Whether every element of an array is a string.

## To allStrings (elems: Seq of Json) -> Bool:
    Repeat for e in elems:
        Inspect e:
            When JStr (s):
                Let ignored be s.
            Otherwise:
                Return false.
    Return true.

## Note
Whether a value has the shape a kind names. An unknown kind matches nothing, so
a mistyped specification fails loudly instead of accepting everything.

## To hasKind (v: Json, kind: Text) -> Bool:
    If kind is equal to "any":
        Return true.
    Inspect v:
        When JNull:
            Return kind is equal to "opttext" or kind is equal to "optint".
        When JBool (b):
            Return kind is equal to "bool".
        When JNum (n):
            Return kind is equal to "int" or kind is equal to "optint".
        When JStr (s):
            Return kind is equal to "text" or kind is equal to "opttext".
        When JArr (elems):
            Return kind is equal to "array" or (kind is equal to "texts" and allStrings(elems)).
        When JObj (entries):
            Return kind is equal to "object".
        Otherwise:
            Return false.
    Return false.

## Note
The first field of an OPEN shape that `v` breaks, or the empty text when it has
the shape. Other fields are allowed: foreign documents grow fields.

## To openShapeProblem (v: Json, specs: Seq of Text) -> Text:
    Inspect v:
        When JObj (entries):
            Let ignored be entries.
        Otherwise:
            Return "expected a JSON object".
    Repeat for spec in specs:
        Let name be fieldName(spec).
        If jsonHas(v, name) is equal to false:
            Return "missing field \"{name}\"".
        If hasKind(jsonGet(v, name), fieldKind(spec)) is equal to false:
            Return "field \"{name}\" is not {fieldKind(spec)}".
    Return "".

## Note
The same for a CLOSED shape: also no field the specification does not name.

## To shapeProblem (v: Json, specs: Seq of Text) -> Text:
    Let mutable names be a new Seq of Text.
    Repeat for spec in specs:
        Push fieldName(spec) to names.
    Inspect jsonNoExtraKeys(v, names):
        When Err (e):
            Return e.
        When Ok (fine):
            Return openShapeProblem(v, specs).
    Return "unreadable".

## Test: a field specification splits into its name and kind

Expect that fieldName("seq:int") is equal to "seq".
Expect that fieldKind("seq:int") is equal to "int".
Expect that fieldKind("payload") is equal to "any".

## Test: a closed shape accepts exactly its fields and names the first wrong one

Let v be jsonParse("{{\"a\": \"x\", \"n\": 3, \"ok\": true, \"tags\": [\"p\"], \"m\": null}}").
Expect that shapeProblem(v, ["a:text", "n:int", "ok:bool", "tags:texts", "m:opttext"]) is equal to "".
Expect that shapeProblem(v, ["a:text", "n:text", "ok:bool", "tags:texts", "m:opttext"]) is equal to "field \"n\" is not text".
Expect that shapeProblem(v, ["a:text"]) is equal to "unexpected key \"n\"".
Expect that shapeProblem(jsonParse("[1]"), ["a:text"]) is equal to "expected a JSON object".

## Test: an open shape tolerates fields it does not name, and a mixed array is not texts

Let v be jsonParse("{{\"a\": \"x\", \"extra\": 1}}").
Expect that openShapeProblem(v, ["a:text"]) is equal to "".
Expect that openShapeProblem(v, ["b:text"]) is equal to "missing field \"b\"".
Expect that hasKind(jsonParse("[\"a\", 1]"), "array") is equal to true.
Expect that hasKind(jsonParse("[\"a\", 1]"), "texts") is equal to false.
Expect that hasKind(v, "mystery") is equal to false.

## Test: a boolean has the bool shape and no other

For all booleans b:
    Expect that hasKind(a new JBool with b b, "bool") is equal to true.
    Expect that hasKind(a new JBool with b b, "int") is equal to false.
